          },
          "text": "2 weeks into my new role at Replit.\n\nI've been a founder for the better part of the last decade, and I've never really worked for a company that wasn't my own or a startup, so naturally, I had some concerns:\n\nHow much freedom would I actually have to experiment? To take initiative, run with ideas, and just build things without asking for permission?\nHow much time would be wasted on internal politics, processes, and other corporate nonsense?\n\n2 weeks in and I'm genuinely blown away.\nInitiative is celebrated. dogfooding is practically a religion and people move ridiculously fast, and there's a palpable bias toward building things rather than talking about building things.\n\nStill early days, obviously, but so far feels like I found my tribe.\n\nS/O to the greatest team:\n@gunnarkolbeins \n@tannerbraden \n@agi2asi \nJacob Fernow"
        },
